# REGRESSION TEST — alias -> DeviceId propagation through `move`.
#
# Bug (now fixed): when a register holding a device ReferenceId was copied into
# another register THROUGH AN ALIAS, the destination lost its "device reference"
# kind and became Unknown. Using it as a device could then raise a false
# "expected a device" error.
#
# Expectation in the dev host: NONE of the lines below show a red error squiggle.

alias deviceRef r1

l r1 d0 ReferenceId      # r1 now holds a device reference (DeviceId)
move r3 deviceRef        # r3 = deviceRef (alias of r1)  -> r3 must stay a DeviceId

# use r3 AS A DEVICE — this is what used to false-error before the fix:
l r4 r3 Temperature
s r3 Setting 1

# --- control: direct register move (always worked) ---
move r5 r1
l r6 r5 Pressure

# --- control: alias of an alias-target still resolves ---
alias deviceRef2 r3
move r7 deviceRef2
l r8 r7 Power
